Done. I built a complete, working terminal Tetris in Rust with ratatui + crossterm.

## What was built

A full Tetris game in `/home/gud/bench-harnesses/results/27b-qwen-1/`, split into focused modules (~1,280 lines including tests):

| File | Responsibility |
|------|----------------|
| `src/main.rs` | Terminal lifecycle + event/gravity loop |
| `src/game.rs` | State machine, movement, rotation + wall kicks, locking, scoring, levels |
| `src/tetromino.rs` | 7 pieces, SRS-style rotation, colours |
| `src/board.rs` | 10×20 field, collision, line clearing |
| `src/input.rs` | Key → action mapping |
| `src/ui.rs` | ratatui rendering (mosaic board, panels, overlays) |

**Features:** 7-bag randomizer, ghost piece, hold slot, next-3 preview, classic scoring (100/300/500/800 × level), level-based speed-up, persistent high score (`~/.tetris-rs-highscore`), pause/restart, coloured UI.

**Controls:** `←/→` move, `↓` soft drop, `Space` hard drop, `↑`/`X` rotate, `Z` rotate ⟲, `C` hold, `P` pause, `R` restart, `Q`/`Esc` quit.

## Run it

```sh
cd /home/gud/bench-harnesses/results/27b-qwen-1
